// meta — declared metaprogramming composites (plan
// 2026-09-22-unified-metaprogramming-layer).
//
// Metaprogramming lives HERE, in the language — never hardcoded in the
// compiler. The compiler carries the EXPANSION MACHINERY
// (src/plugin/composite.rs); the shapes live in `.bv` files (Golden Rule
// 24, docs/architecture/proof-vs-shape.md).

// `execute_many!(call1, call2, ...)` — sequential call emission (SPEC
// §18.2). The `...` rest parameter binds ALL trailing arguments as the
// sanctioned compile-time iteration channel: a `foreach` over it unrolls
// at expansion, one emission per argument — N = arg count, known only at
// compile time. Supersedes the retired Rust-side `execute_many!` macro
// (2026-09-18): the composite reaches the same behavior in the language.
$defn execute_many(...calls: Expr) {
    foreach c in calls {
        c;
    }
};